1)forge test(in main folder like in sec-2)

and if we have Counter.t.sol then it will compile all our code and it will run test from test file









We have the test/ folder in Foundry because automated testing is the single most important part of smart contract development.

Once a smart contract is deployed to a real blockchain like Ethereum, its code is immutable—meaning it cannot be changed, patched, or updated if you find a bug later. If there is a flaw in your code, a hacker can drain all the funds instantly.




When you run the command forge test in your terminal, Forge scans your test/ folder, looks for any files ending in .t.sol, runs every function that starts with the word test, and gives you a clean green checkmark if your logic is secure.

*/